course: dictionary
lesson: 15725
title: Transatlantic: across the ocean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word transatlantic is made of two parts. Trans means across, and Atlantic is the name of an ocean. So transatlantic means across the Atlantic Ocean. «We took a transatlantic flight to visit our cousins in New York.» A flight that crosses the Atlantic is transatlantic.
explain: The word can also describe things on both sides of the ocean. «Our transatlantic call to Grandma in Canada crackled, but we could still hear her laughing.» The call linked two sides of the ocean, so it was transatlantic.
explain: Trans is a useful clue in other words too. A transport carries things from place to place, and a transfer moves something across to somewhere new. When you meet a new word, check its parts, then check the sentence.
fact: Transatlantic means crossing the Atlantic Ocean, such as a flight or voyage between Europe and America.
fact: Transatlantic also means about or between the countries on both sides of the Atlantic, like the UK and the USA.
fact: «A transatlantic flight» is a flight that crosses the Atlantic Ocean.
fact: In history, the first transatlantic flight and the first transatlantic telegraph cable were big steps in travel and communication.
fact: The transatlantic slave trade was a terrible trade in enslaved African people, and you will learn about it in history lessons.
exercise: «The transatlantic flight took many hours to reach New York.» What does transatlantic mean here? | Going round the city ring road | Crossing the Pacific Ocean | *Crossing the Atlantic Ocean | Crossing the Sahara desert
exercise: Dad says, «Our transatlantic call to Grandma was late at night.» Why is it called transatlantic? | Because it happened in a café | Because Grandma has a big car | Because it was sung in a song | *Because it linked two countries on opposite sides of the Atlantic
exercise: A transatlantic voyage links which two places? | Africa and Antarctica | Two towns in the same country | Asia and Australia | *Europe and America
test: «The transatlantic telegraph cable carried messages under the sea.» What does transatlantic mean? | Very quick and fast | *Crossing the Atlantic Ocean | Under a mountain | Inside a school
test: «The two countries agreed a transatlantic trade deal.» What does this tell you? | The deal is about a small village | The deal is about fish in the ocean | The deal was signed in a swimming pool | *The deal is between countries on both sides of the Atlantic
exam: Which sentence uses transatlantic correctly? | My transatlantic bedroom is painted blue. | I walked across the playground at break. | *Our transatlantic flight landed in New York after crossing the ocean. | The transatlantic sandwich was very tasty.
